{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
  "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore B. Olson",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents dispute the wisdom, efficacy, and constitutionality of Ohio's franchise tax system, but they face two insurmountable obstacles in this Court. First, they cannot demonstrate any actual, concrete, and direct injury as a result of Ohio's investment tax credit to satisfy the irreducible minimum requirement for standing in this Court. Secondly, the facial Dormant Commerce Clause challenge that they bring is without merit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson, who would have -- who would have standing? I understand your argument that Ohio taxpayers don't, but are there people who would have standing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think there has to be somebody who can challenge it, though."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Douglas R. Cole",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We agree with DaimlerChrysler's position, both as to standing and as to the merits. The Respondents' grievance as taxpayers, the sole standing argument they press here, is a textbook example of the generalized public grievance that the Court has repeatedly rejected as a basis for -- or for standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Douglas R. Cole",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do, however, dispute whether or not that gives them standing to also challenge the ITC."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question? Would the case be any different if, instead of a tax credit, they offered a cash subsidy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ohio",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ohio respectfully urges the Court to reverse the decision below or, in the alternative, to vacate the decision for lack of standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Enrich",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The discrimination here is not between those businesses which are not present at all in Ohio and those which are doing their manufacturing in Ohio, the discrimination is between those who are doing business in Ohio, but not locating their new manufacturing activity in Ohio, and those who do business in Ohio, but do locate their new manufacturing activity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask you the same question I asked your adversary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1704",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4906558c4deb55aeede93c723ac2fb629c3e5ce686414d54f688ec7c95dcc40c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4906558c4deb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "discriminatory distinction between out-of-State businesses who are subjected to the tax, in the case of the Ohio investment tax credit, and in-State businesses, which are excused from paying that same tax, which is, again, exactly what a tariff does, Your Honor."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
